-- Account deletion and memory erasure (#303, part 3 of #31; docs/engineering/data-lifecycle.md,
-- audit.md "Anonymisation"). Generated part: audit_event.actor_ref and its actor index, the
-- audit_actor_salt table, and user foreign keys that keep workspace data when a user is deleted
-- (blob.created_by, matter_restriction.created_by, workspace_feature_flag.updated_by and
-- legal_ack_by become nullable ON DELETE SET NULL; blob.created_by used to cascade).
-- Hand edits:
--   * audit_actor_salt is global and owner-only: no privileges for causedeck_app or the clerk role;
--     only the SECURITY DEFINER functions below read or write it.
--   * app_audit_actor_ref(user): the per-user salted ref (hex sha256(salt || uuid bytes)), creating
--     the salt on first use. Internal (no grant). app_audit_actor_ref_matches(user, ref) checks a
--     ref without creating a salt, for the verifiers.
--   * Chain verification before anything changes: every chain (each workspace and the account
--     chain) is checked with the 0008 canonical form, and the migration aborts on a broken chain,
--     so the re-chain below cannot launder tampering.
--   * app_audit_canonical v2: a row with actor_ref hashes 'actor_ref' in place of 'actor_user_id';
--     a row without it (no actor) keeps the 0008 form unchanged.
--   * app_audit_append (same signature and grants) stores actor_ref for every user actor.
--   * One-time re-chain: legacy rows get actor_ref and every chain's hashes are recomputed in chain
--     order (the oldest surviving row's prev_hash is kept as given, as verifyChain does).
--   * app_audit_immutable additionally allows (a) the anonymise update, which nulls actor_user_id
--     on a row with actor_ref and changes nothing else, while app.audit_anonymise is 'on', and (b)
--     the re-chain update (actor_ref, prev_hash, hash only) while app.audit_rechain is 'on'. The app
--     role still has no UPDATE privilege; owner_definer_anonymise backs the owner under FORCE RLS.
--   * app_audit_anonymise_actor(user): refuses while the user row exists, nulls actor_user_id in
--     every chain, deletes the salt (the ref can no longer be recomputed) and returns the count.
--   * app_audit_verify_account_chain also reports 'actor' when actor_user_id does not match
--     actor_ref (same return shape).
--   * deletion_job account_self: account deletion jobs (no workspace) for the current user, while
--     no workspace is pinned; ws_isolation never matches a null workspace_id.
--   * Additive or replace-compatible: the previous release's calls keep working.
CREATE TABLE "audit_actor_salt" (
	"user_id" uuid PRIMARY KEY NOT NULL,
	"salt" "bytea" NOT NULL,
	"created_at" timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL
);
